1
00:00:00,834 --> 00:00:04,504
[theme music playing]

2
00:00:11,261 --> 00:00:13,930
[Claire] <i>You've done a number of</i>
<i>unspeakable things in the past,</i>

3
00:00:14,014 --> 00:00:16,182
<i>and I never said anything about it.</i>

4
00:00:16,266 --> 00:00:20,228
<i>But to have another woman raped?</i>
<i>That's unacceptable.</i>

5
00:00:20,979 --> 00:00:25,358
[Julio] <i>Don't treat Miss Aguas</i>
<i>like Raul's mistresses</i>

6
00:00:25,442 --> 00:00:27,694
<i>that you can easily get rid of.</i>

7
00:00:27,777 --> 00:00:30,780
<i>If Arnaldo finds out about what you did,</i>

8
00:00:30,864 --> 00:00:32,782
<i>your son won't be able to forgive you.</i>

9
00:00:32,866 --> 00:00:35,785
[Ivy] <i>Even if you don't tell me</i>
<i>who's behind this,</i>

10
00:00:35,869 --> 00:00:37,787
-<i>I know you work for Emilia!</i>
-[gunshots]

11
00:00:37,871 --> 00:00:38,913
<i>Tell Emilia…</i>

12
00:00:38,997 --> 00:00:41,708
-[Diego] <i>Let's go!</i>
-<i>I'm not afraid of her!</i>

13
00:00:41,791 --> 00:00:44,169
[Diego] <i>Ivy, I want you to be happy.</i>

14
00:00:44,252 --> 00:00:47,797
<i>I want you to be free from this burden.</i>

15
00:00:47,881 --> 00:00:50,550
<i>You know how much I love you, right?</i>

16
00:00:50,633 --> 00:00:52,385
[Ivy] <i>Diego, I love you.</i>

17
00:00:52,802 --> 00:00:56,056
[Arnaldo] <i>I won't file for that</i>
<i>damn candidacy until I find Ivy.</i>

18
00:00:56,139 --> 00:00:58,266
<i>You know, that woman's</i>
<i>trying to brainwash you.</i>

19
00:00:58,349 --> 00:01:00,435
<i>Ivy isn't the problem. You are!</i>

20
00:01:00,518 --> 00:01:02,896
<i>Because I despise that woman.</i>

21
00:01:02,979 --> 00:01:04,856
<i>You know, I'm like a mad dog</i>

22
00:01:04,939 --> 00:01:07,650
<i>dying to shred her into pieces</i>
<i>every time I see her!</i>

23
00:01:08,985 --> 00:01:12,906
[Ivy] <i>I'm here to show you that</i>
<i>I am very much alive and well.</i>

24
00:01:12,989 --> 00:01:15,075
[Arnaldo] <i>Let go! Let go!</i>
<i>What the hell is wrong with you two?</i>

25
00:01:15,158 --> 00:01:17,911
[Ivy] <i>She sent her men to try and rape me!</i>

26
00:01:17,994 --> 00:01:21,039
[Nimfa] <i>I know</i>
<i>where Camia's funds are hidden.</i>

27
00:01:21,581 --> 00:01:23,792
<i>They came from an anonymous donor.</i>

28
00:01:23,875 --> 00:01:26,711
[Emilia] <i>Okay, just make sure</i>
<i>you keep your promise</i>

29
00:01:26,795 --> 00:01:29,047
<i>before I keep mine.</i>

30
00:01:29,130 --> 00:01:30,715
[Arnaldo] <i>She will not get away with this.</i>

31
00:01:30,799 --> 00:01:31,549
<i>Get away from me.</i>

32
00:01:31,633 --> 00:01:32,759
<i>-What's wrong?</i>
<i>-Get away, Arnaldo!</i>

33
00:01:32,842 --> 00:01:34,302
<i>-What's with you?!</i>
<i>-Get away!</i>

34
00:01:34,385 --> 00:01:36,805
[Arnaldo] <i>Given you're in shock,</i>
<i>I will go the extra mile</i>

35
00:01:36,888 --> 00:01:38,932
<i>to understand you. Rest for tonight,</i>

36
00:01:39,015 --> 00:01:41,893
<i>so you can come with me</i>
<i>when I file for candidacy.</i>

37
00:01:44,813 --> 00:01:47,857
[suspenseful music playing]

38
00:01:57,242 --> 00:01:58,409
-Guard.
-Sir?

39
00:01:58,493 --> 00:02:00,411
-Good evening.
-Good evening, sir.

40
00:02:00,495 --> 00:02:02,288
Where can I find the Serendipity Room?

41
00:02:02,372 --> 00:02:05,416
I think you're looking for
the Serenity Room, sir.

42
00:02:05,500 --> 00:02:06,501
It's over there.

43
00:02:08,002 --> 00:02:12,799
You're Diego Torillo, right?
The one running for governor?

44
00:02:12,882 --> 00:02:13,883
Yes, that's me.

45
00:02:14,342 --> 00:02:17,178
Whatever you're up to, please
don't push through with it.

46
00:02:17,262 --> 00:02:20,223
I know you're here
to investigate the Ardientes.

47
00:02:20,306 --> 00:02:22,517
You don't know what
that family's capable of.

48
00:02:22,600 --> 00:02:24,144
I can take care of myself.

49
00:02:24,519 --> 00:02:26,771
Not everyone is as brave as you, sir.

50
00:02:26,855 --> 00:02:28,356
If you push through with your plans,

51
00:02:28,439 --> 00:02:32,527
I'll get in trouble for sure.
So, please just leave, sir.

52
00:02:34,237 --> 00:02:36,239
[tense music playing]

53
00:02:42,245 --> 00:02:43,288
[grunts]

54
00:02:48,626 --> 00:02:51,212
-Is that all there is?
-Congressman…

55
00:02:51,504 --> 00:02:53,798
we don't have enough men.
That's why business is slow.

56
00:02:53,882 --> 00:02:56,843
Last I heard, our men
are now working for Jaguar.

57
00:02:59,262 --> 00:03:02,223
That Jaguar sure is testing my patience.

58
00:03:02,307 --> 00:03:04,934
[Domingo] Congressman,
should I make arrangements

59
00:03:05,018 --> 00:03:06,686
for your meeting?

60
00:03:06,769 --> 00:03:07,854
[chuckles]

61
00:03:09,230 --> 00:03:11,107
Let me ask you, Domingo.

62
00:03:12,317 --> 00:03:15,153
If you find yourself
in the middle of battle,

63
00:03:15,236 --> 00:03:18,364
and you see your troops
switching their allegiance,

64
00:03:18,448 --> 00:03:22,410
will you talk to your enemy?

65
00:03:22,493 --> 00:03:25,288
-[Domingo] No, Congressman.
-That answers your question.

66
00:03:25,371 --> 00:03:27,916
Talking to your enemy…

67
00:03:28,750 --> 00:03:32,712
is tantamount to declaring surrender.

68
00:03:32,795 --> 00:03:34,172
I must admit…

69
00:03:34,255 --> 00:03:38,635
Jaguar has affected our operations.

70
00:03:39,260 --> 00:03:42,722
But this isn't my only source
of livelihood.

71
00:03:42,805 --> 00:03:45,850
I still have a lot of money.
I have lots of it.

72
00:03:46,851 --> 00:03:50,855
I am not Julio Ardiente for nothing!

73
00:03:50,939 --> 00:03:53,024
Now, as for Jaguar…

74
00:03:53,107 --> 00:03:54,484
He's the one who's insignificant.

75
00:03:54,567 --> 00:03:59,906
He's nothing but a cheap gangster

76
00:03:59,989 --> 00:04:02,200
with a cheesy name.

77
00:04:02,283 --> 00:04:03,493
For now…

78
00:04:04,202 --> 00:04:08,331
let's allow him to think
he's winning the battle.

79
00:04:08,414 --> 00:04:12,919
But at the proper time,
I'll show that Jaguar…

80
00:04:14,629 --> 00:04:17,882
who the real king of this jungle is.

81
00:04:19,342 --> 00:04:22,679
[dramatic music playing]

82
00:04:38,486 --> 00:04:42,031
[Marlon] Everyone, thank you
for your time.

83
00:04:42,115 --> 00:04:44,742
Now, I ask you to help
prepare the materials

84
00:04:44,826 --> 00:04:46,828
for Diego's filing of candidacy tomorrow.

85
00:04:46,911 --> 00:04:50,790
All of Diego's supporters need
to be there tomorrow,

86
00:04:50,873 --> 00:04:53,042
so we can show the Ardientes
how big our group is!

87
00:04:53,126 --> 00:04:54,168
-That's right!
-[woman] That's right!

88
00:04:54,252 --> 00:04:56,921
We are doing this for Diego Torillo!

89
00:04:57,005 --> 00:04:59,590
And we're doing this for the new Ardiente!

90
00:04:59,674 --> 00:05:00,466
[Camia] Yes!

91
00:05:00,550 --> 00:05:02,760
Diego Torillo for the new Ardiente!

92
00:05:02,844 --> 00:05:05,722
[all] Diego Torillo for the new Ardiente!

93
00:05:05,805 --> 00:05:07,056
-[Marlon] Thank you!
-[applause]

94
00:05:07,140 --> 00:05:11,227
Get some rest, because you need
to look your best tomorrow.

95
00:05:11,311 --> 00:05:15,023
I'm sure the ladies will want
to take selfies with you.

96
00:05:15,106 --> 00:05:16,983
And try flirting with them too.

97
00:05:17,066 --> 00:05:19,360
Batch, you're at it again.

98
00:05:19,861 --> 00:05:22,113
I remember you were
a ladies' man in college.

99
00:05:22,196 --> 00:05:23,740
[Marlon laughs]

100
00:05:23,823 --> 00:05:27,160
[Marlon] Bro, charm trumps
intelligence every time.

101
00:05:27,243 --> 00:05:31,205
Why do you think the Ardientes
are still in power?

102
00:05:31,289 --> 00:05:33,750
And whether you admit it or not,
your grandfather

103
00:05:33,833 --> 00:05:35,168
and your brother are very charismatic.

104
00:05:35,251 --> 00:05:37,795
That's why they're still
in power. You'll need that.

105
00:05:37,879 --> 00:05:42,675
Batch, if your heart sincerely
wants to serve the people,

106
00:05:42,759 --> 00:05:44,844
you don't need to pretend
to be someone you're not.

107
00:05:48,389 --> 00:05:50,349
[tense music playing]

108
00:05:50,808 --> 00:05:53,436
-[Marlon] All right, bro!
-Take care. Thank you so much.

109
00:05:53,519 --> 00:05:55,438
-Remember to vote for him, okay?
-Tomorrow.

110
00:05:55,521 --> 00:05:56,606
-Yes.
-Are you all right?

111
00:05:56,689 --> 00:05:57,774
Don't listen to him too much, okay?

112
00:05:57,857 --> 00:06:00,401
You heard him.
I'm no good at teaching stuff.

113
00:06:00,485 --> 00:06:03,905
-Are you guys all right?
-[woman] He's so handsome.

114
00:06:03,988 --> 00:06:05,239
-[Marlon] He's Chris.
-[man] Okay.

115
00:06:05,323 --> 00:06:06,365
-[Marlon] Okay.
-[Camia] That looks okay.

116
00:06:06,449 --> 00:06:07,784
-[man] Fix those.
-[Marlon] Okay.

117
00:06:07,867 --> 00:06:09,160
[applause]

118
00:06:09,744 --> 00:06:11,162
[Marlon] Take care of them.

119
00:06:12,121 --> 00:06:13,414
Okay. Very good!

120
00:06:15,625 --> 00:06:16,793
Auntie, are you all right?

121
00:06:16,876 --> 00:06:17,877
[woman] Yes.

122
00:06:18,377 --> 00:06:20,046
-What's up, Mike?
-Everything's set, Diego.

123
00:06:20,129 --> 00:06:22,799
-Yes, Diego, we're all set.
-Are we ready for tomorrow?

124
00:06:22,882 --> 00:06:23,800
We're ready.

125
00:06:23,883 --> 00:06:24,926
-You sure?
-We can do this!

126
00:06:25,009 --> 00:06:26,010
[man] Of course!

127
00:06:29,764 --> 00:06:33,935
Mayor, you need to sign
this for the campaign.

128
00:06:34,602 --> 00:06:36,479
-Do you have the other one?
-Yes, everything's here.

129
00:06:40,358 --> 00:06:42,026
-[Diego] What's up?
-[Mike] Diego!

130
00:06:42,110 --> 00:06:45,279
-Mike, are you all right?
-[man] You're going to win!

131
00:06:45,363 --> 00:06:47,281
-Aunt Camia.
-You're a man of the people.

132
00:06:47,365 --> 00:06:49,117
-Nimfa.
-[indistinct chatter]

133
00:06:49,200 --> 00:06:51,536
Are you ready for tomorrow?

134
00:06:51,619 --> 00:06:54,872
[Pandoy] We'll do everything
to make those Ardientes lose.

135
00:06:56,290 --> 00:06:57,667
-[Arnaldo] Is that it?
-[man] Yes.

136
00:06:57,750 --> 00:07:01,879
Fix that up. I don't like that. Change it.

137
00:07:02,755 --> 00:07:07,426
[Arnaldo] Fans and hats?
We need more of these.

138
00:07:09,512 --> 00:07:12,056
[Diego] Here, let's roll these up.

139
00:07:12,140 --> 00:07:14,308
-Let me help you.
-[man] Please roll those up.

140
00:07:14,392 --> 00:07:16,310
[Camia] Let's tidy these up
so we can get some rest.

141
00:07:16,394 --> 00:07:19,105
-Let's roll it up.
-No. I can do it, Nimfa.

142
00:07:21,816 --> 00:07:23,693
[tense music playing]

143
00:07:24,610 --> 00:07:25,903
[unintelligible]

144
00:07:25,987 --> 00:07:27,905
-[Camia] There we go.
-All set.

145
00:07:31,033 --> 00:07:33,369
ARNALDO: A TRUE ARDIENTE,
A MAN OF GENUINE COMPASSION

146
00:07:34,495 --> 00:07:35,788
[Arnaldo] I want a bigger tarpaulin.

147
00:07:35,872 --> 00:07:37,165
Print something bigger than this.

148
00:07:37,248 --> 00:07:39,041
-[man] We need a bigger tarp.
-Okay?

149
00:07:39,125 --> 00:07:40,585
[man] Is this the largest size?

150
00:07:40,668 --> 00:07:42,253
The mayor wants something bigger.

151
00:07:42,879 --> 00:07:43,880
All right.

152
00:07:54,140 --> 00:07:55,933
-[Diego] Here.
-[man] We're ready for tomorrow.

153
00:07:56,017 --> 00:07:57,018
[indistinct chatter]

154
00:07:58,227 --> 00:07:59,645
We don't have something to tie it with.

155
00:07:59,729 --> 00:08:01,272
-Batch.
-Batch.

156
00:08:01,355 --> 00:08:03,399
-Where's the…
-[Diego] You're at it again.

157
00:08:03,483 --> 00:08:04,859
I'll just help them.

158
00:08:05,943 --> 00:08:07,278
[indistinct chatter]

159
00:08:07,361 --> 00:08:08,488
There it is!

160
00:08:09,363 --> 00:08:10,865
He's just going to bother you.

161
00:08:22,251 --> 00:08:24,253
-[sensual music playing]
-[Emilia moans]

162
00:08:25,254 --> 00:08:28,799
-Raul. What are you doing?
-Yes?

163
00:08:28,883 --> 00:08:29,759
What?

164
00:08:31,010 --> 00:08:32,136
What are you doing?

165
00:08:33,763 --> 00:08:37,141
Nothing. I just know that
you've been exhausted lately,

166
00:08:37,225 --> 00:08:39,602
from all the campaigning for your son.

167
00:08:39,685 --> 00:08:41,854
Then there's Ivy Aguas…

168
00:08:42,355 --> 00:08:44,232
who's been giving you nothing but stress.

169
00:08:45,233 --> 00:08:46,984
Plus there's Papa.

170
00:08:47,068 --> 00:08:51,280
He didn't give us his blessing
to renew our vows.

171
00:08:52,240 --> 00:08:57,245
But… I vow to love you,
until the end of time, Emilia.

172
00:08:57,662 --> 00:08:58,788
Oh.

173
00:08:59,497 --> 00:09:00,790
I love you too.

174
00:09:03,626 --> 00:09:05,169
Breakfast in bed?

175
00:09:05,253 --> 00:09:07,880
-What?
-Here. I prepared it for you.

176
00:09:08,756 --> 00:09:09,757
[sighs]

177
00:09:11,884 --> 00:09:13,094
I made that.

178
00:09:15,763 --> 00:09:16,806
[Raul chuckles]

179
00:09:16,889 --> 00:09:20,685
-[giggles] This is too much.
-What? You don't want to eat?

180
00:09:20,768 --> 00:09:22,562
No. But that's really sweet of you.

181
00:09:22,645 --> 00:09:25,648
But are you happy?
It doesn't look like it.

182
00:09:25,731 --> 00:09:27,900
It seems like you want
to eat something else.

183
00:09:27,984 --> 00:09:29,735
[both laughing]

184
00:09:29,819 --> 00:09:33,155
Well, I would love to. But…

185
00:09:33,239 --> 00:09:36,242
-we have a long day today.
-Okay. What?

186
00:09:36,867 --> 00:09:39,203
We have a lot to do today.

187
00:09:39,287 --> 00:09:40,997
-[Emilia] Right?
-[Raul] And so?

188
00:09:42,456 --> 00:09:43,457
[Emilia moans]

189
00:09:46,210 --> 00:09:48,254
[tense music playing]

190
00:09:52,300 --> 00:09:54,010
[laughs]

191
00:09:54,093 --> 00:09:56,721
Why are your fingers so dirty?

192
00:09:56,804 --> 00:09:58,055
-You should cut your nails.
-Is this dirty?

193
00:09:58,139 --> 00:09:58,931
Ew!

194
00:09:59,765 --> 00:10:01,934
Come on. It's just dirt.

195
00:10:02,393 --> 00:10:03,352
Oh.

196
00:10:03,436 --> 00:10:04,729
Let's eat.

197
00:10:04,812 --> 00:10:06,647
-[laughs]
-Okay?

198
00:10:16,949 --> 00:10:20,494
[ominous music playing]

199
00:10:24,874 --> 00:10:25,875
[groans]

200
00:10:26,626 --> 00:10:28,878
[ominous music playing]

201
00:10:31,005 --> 00:10:32,923
[screams]

202
00:10:34,508 --> 00:10:35,509
[screams]

203
00:10:36,093 --> 00:10:38,471
[groaning]

204
00:10:38,846 --> 00:10:39,847
Help!

205
00:10:43,517 --> 00:10:45,936
[groaning]

206
00:10:46,812 --> 00:10:47,813
Get them off me!

207
00:10:48,856 --> 00:10:50,816
[screams] Help!

208
00:10:52,234 --> 00:10:54,820
Grandpa? Grandpa?!

209
00:10:56,113 --> 00:10:58,824
-That was Papa!
-Wait.

210
00:10:59,325 --> 00:11:00,660
[coughing]

211
00:11:00,743 --> 00:11:02,578
-Grandpa!
-Ouch! Ouch!

212
00:11:02,662 --> 00:11:05,915
Grandpa, get up.

213
00:11:05,998 --> 00:11:07,291
[both groaning]

214
00:11:08,125 --> 00:11:12,129
Arnaldo, call the guards!
How did that get in here?!

215
00:11:13,631 --> 00:11:17,802
Papa! What's happening?!
Oh, my! What's this mess?!

216
00:11:17,885 --> 00:11:20,179
[Julio] Call all our guards!

217
00:11:20,471 --> 00:11:23,724
Who brought that in here?! Tell me!

218
00:11:23,808 --> 00:11:25,559
-Ouch!
-[Emilia screams]

219
00:11:25,643 --> 00:11:28,437
-What's happening, Papa?
-It hurts! It hurts! It hurts!

220
00:11:29,480 --> 00:11:31,399
[Arnaldo] I think you need
to take a shower.

221
00:11:32,066 --> 00:11:33,567
[Emilia] Get rid of those!

222
00:11:35,694 --> 00:11:37,738
[dramatic music playing]

223
00:11:44,829 --> 00:11:46,872
[pensive music playing]

224
00:11:49,667 --> 00:11:51,961
ARDIENTE BROTHERS TO FILE CANDIDACY

225
00:11:54,839 --> 00:11:55,881
[phone ringing]

226
00:11:59,635 --> 00:12:01,303
-Mom?
-[Camia sighs]

227
00:12:01,387 --> 00:12:03,055
I can't believe that Emilia!

228
00:12:03,139 --> 00:12:05,766
Diego told me what she did.

229
00:12:06,350 --> 00:12:07,685
I want to see you.

230
00:12:08,436 --> 00:12:10,271
Calm down, Mom.

231
00:12:10,354 --> 00:12:12,022
<i>We'll get our chance</i>

232
00:12:12,106 --> 00:12:14,733
to expose Emilia's true colors,

233
00:12:14,817 --> 00:12:16,694
<i>but you have to calm down.</i>

234
00:12:16,777 --> 00:12:19,363
When you see her later,

235
00:12:19,447 --> 00:12:22,116
she can't suspect that you know anything.

236
00:12:22,616 --> 00:12:23,909
I know that, Lily.

237
00:12:24,535 --> 00:12:26,912
Is Arnaldo filing his candidacy later too?

238
00:12:26,996 --> 00:12:29,165
Yes, Mom. It's complicated.

239
00:12:29,248 --> 00:12:31,500
<i>Maybe we should meet up.</i>

240
00:12:31,584 --> 00:12:32,918
You know the drill.

241
00:12:33,002 --> 00:12:34,044
<i>Be safe, Mom.</i>

242
00:12:34,128 --> 00:12:36,589
I will, dear. Especially now.

243
00:12:41,218 --> 00:12:43,471
[tense music playing]

244
00:12:45,931 --> 00:12:48,559
[Camia] Nimfa, I'm going
to the cooperative, okay?

245
00:12:48,642 --> 00:12:49,643
I'll see you later.

246
00:12:49,727 --> 00:12:51,770
Do you want me to go
with you now, Miss Camia?

247
00:12:51,854 --> 00:12:53,939
I have nowhere else to be, anyway.

248
00:12:54,023 --> 00:12:56,484
No, thanks. I'll be fine.

249
00:12:56,567 --> 00:12:58,861
Besides, I have my bodyguards with me.

250
00:12:59,737 --> 00:13:01,822
How do you plan on going to the rally?

251
00:13:01,906 --> 00:13:03,908
[chuckles] You don't have
to worry about me.

252
00:13:03,991 --> 00:13:05,993
I'll figure it out.

253
00:13:06,076 --> 00:13:09,955
I'm sure I won't get lost.
I'm from around here, after all.

254
00:13:10,748 --> 00:13:12,750
But, you should take care, Miss Camia.

255
00:13:12,833 --> 00:13:15,461
It seems like the Ardientes
have it out for you.

256
00:13:17,838 --> 00:13:20,674
-I'll see you later.
-Take care!

257
00:13:23,677 --> 00:13:26,639
[foreboding music playing]

258
00:13:30,851 --> 00:13:32,811
[suspenseful music playing]

259
00:13:41,612 --> 00:13:42,613
[groans]

260
00:13:51,038 --> 00:13:54,542
Uh… Wait here.
I just left something upstairs.

261
00:14:02,758 --> 00:14:05,344
[suspenseful music playing]

262
00:14:13,894 --> 00:14:16,855
[tense music plays]

263
00:14:23,612 --> 00:14:24,780
[phone rings]

264
00:14:26,365 --> 00:14:27,408
Mom?

265
00:14:27,491 --> 00:14:28,492
[Camia] <i>Lily.</i>

266
00:14:28,826 --> 00:14:30,828
I can't meet you today.

267
00:14:31,829 --> 00:14:33,664
-Why not?
-It's Nimfa…

268
00:14:33,747 --> 00:14:35,249
<i>She's going through my things.</i>

269
00:14:35,332 --> 00:14:37,251
I need to deal with this first.

270
00:14:37,334 --> 00:14:39,128
She's doing what?

271
00:14:39,211 --> 00:14:41,630
[tense music playing]

272
00:14:44,049 --> 00:14:45,050
Nimfa!

273
00:14:47,177 --> 00:14:49,346
-What are you doing?!
-[quietly] Miss Camia…

274
00:14:49,430 --> 00:14:53,225
[dramatic music playing]

275
00:14:55,227 --> 00:14:58,272
I've noticed just how nosy
you can be, Nimfa.

276
00:14:58,355 --> 00:15:00,733
But how can you go through my things?!

277
00:15:01,859 --> 00:15:04,653
[sighs] This is unforgivable, Nimfa!

278
00:15:06,071 --> 00:15:08,782
Please forgive me, Miss Camia. [gasps]

279
00:15:08,866 --> 00:15:10,576
I won't do it again!

280
00:15:11,744 --> 00:15:16,290
I have a confession to make.
Please hear me out.

281
00:15:18,667 --> 00:15:22,171
I just really need some money.

282
00:15:23,005 --> 00:15:27,176
My father is sick.
That's why he isn't here.

283
00:15:27,259 --> 00:15:32,056
Because he needs treatment.
Please forgive me, Miss Camia!

284
00:15:32,139 --> 00:15:33,682
[sobbing]

285
00:15:34,642 --> 00:15:37,019
Nimfa, why didn't you tell me this before?

286
00:15:37,728 --> 00:15:41,523
I could've helped you.
You shouldn't have done this.

287
00:15:42,858 --> 00:15:45,945
But you've already done so much for me.

288
00:15:46,612 --> 00:15:50,282
I couldn't dare ask any more from you.

289
00:15:51,992 --> 00:15:54,203
Dad needs to undergo an operation.

290
00:15:55,371 --> 00:15:58,165
We need a huge amount of money.

291
00:15:58,248 --> 00:16:01,794
I didn't know what else to do, Miss Camia.

292
00:16:02,127 --> 00:16:03,337
I'll help you.

293
00:16:04,213 --> 00:16:05,881
I'll give you money.

294
00:16:06,715 --> 00:16:08,425
But what you did was wrong.

295
00:16:09,468 --> 00:16:10,427
<i>And I don't know…</i>

296
00:16:10,511 --> 00:16:12,846
if I can still trust you after this.

297
00:16:13,514 --> 00:16:16,809
Miss Camia, I'm begging you!

298
00:16:16,892 --> 00:16:21,271
Please don't fire me.
I really need this job.

299
00:16:21,814 --> 00:16:23,524
This is my only source of income.

300
00:16:23,607 --> 00:16:28,404
I've got no job other than this.
I'm begging you!

301
00:16:28,487 --> 00:16:31,490
<i>This is my only hope.</i>

302
00:16:31,573 --> 00:16:34,660
I didn't know what to do, Miss Camia.

303
00:16:34,743 --> 00:16:38,247
I'm sorry, Miss Camia. I really am.

304
00:16:39,164 --> 00:16:40,958
Please forgive me.

305
00:16:41,500 --> 00:16:43,085
I'm so sorry.

306
00:16:45,129 --> 00:16:47,506
[sobbing]

307
00:16:49,591 --> 00:16:50,801
What?!

308
00:16:50,884 --> 00:16:54,722
Camia caught me.
I need to be extra careful.

309
00:16:55,347 --> 00:16:57,641
I'm going to lie low for now.

310
00:16:58,517 --> 00:17:01,395
My goodness! What about
the things you've always wanted?

311
00:17:01,478 --> 00:17:03,897
The money, the jewelry, and the car?

312
00:17:03,981 --> 00:17:06,942
What? Do you want to be
poor all your life?

313
00:17:07,026 --> 00:17:09,445
Ma'am, calm down.

314
00:17:09,820 --> 00:17:11,071
[Emilia] <i>How can I calm down…</i>

315
00:17:11,155 --> 00:17:14,783
now that Camia knows
you've been spying on her?

316
00:17:14,867 --> 00:17:16,744
So how are we going to prove

317
00:17:16,827 --> 00:17:18,912
that she's connected to Ivy Aguas?

318
00:17:18,996 --> 00:17:20,664
[sighs] <i>Okay. Never mind.</i>

319
00:17:20,748 --> 00:17:23,292
Keep it low-key.
This is what you're going to do.

320
00:17:23,584 --> 00:17:28,505
Since Diego will file for candidacy soon…

321
00:17:28,589 --> 00:17:32,051
<i>I want you to sneak in</i>
<i>and sabotage it, okay?</i>

322
00:17:32,134 --> 00:17:36,430
-I want to cripple them all.
-Hold on, ma'am.

323
00:17:36,513 --> 00:17:38,682
That wasn't part of our agreement.

324
00:17:38,766 --> 00:17:41,310
<i>I only agreed to spy on them.</i>

325
00:17:41,393 --> 00:17:44,980
[chuckles] How about you give me
some incentives?

326
00:17:45,064 --> 00:17:47,274
Do your task first.

327
00:17:47,357 --> 00:17:50,110
Then, I'll give you a down payment.

328
00:17:50,194 --> 00:17:51,278
[chuckles]

329
00:17:51,361 --> 00:17:52,362
Yes!

330
00:17:53,322 --> 00:17:55,657
<i>You'll be surprised, ma'am.</i>

331
00:17:56,241 --> 00:17:59,453
I can say that it'll be a blast.

332
00:17:59,995 --> 00:18:01,538
Make sure of that.

333
00:18:03,749 --> 00:18:06,210
[tense music playing]

334
00:18:10,839 --> 00:18:11,965
-[Emilia] Papa.
-Ouch!

335
00:18:12,049 --> 00:18:14,051
You're welcome to stay here
in our room first,

336
00:18:14,134 --> 00:18:16,553
while the maids clean up your room.

337
00:18:16,637 --> 00:18:17,805
Stay here.

338
00:18:18,889 --> 00:18:22,101
Never mind. Doctor. Don't worry about it.

339
00:18:22,768 --> 00:18:24,645
It's nothing. I'm going to be fine.

340
00:18:24,728 --> 00:18:28,524
These are just bites by these ants, okay?

341
00:18:28,857 --> 00:18:31,193
You already prescribed
an ointment and some medicine,

342
00:18:31,276 --> 00:18:32,402
I'll just take them.

343
00:18:32,486 --> 00:18:37,282
You might have other patients
to attend to.

344
00:18:39,076 --> 00:18:40,077
[sighs]

345
00:18:42,579 --> 00:18:46,917
I will kill whoever did this to me.

346
00:18:47,751 --> 00:18:49,169
I'm going to crush his larynx,

347
00:18:49,253 --> 00:18:52,131
that he may never speak nor talk again!

348
00:18:52,756 --> 00:18:55,050
What did the guards say?

349
00:18:55,134 --> 00:18:58,303
[Raul] Um, nothing showed up
on the CCTV, Papa.

350
00:18:58,387 --> 00:19:00,139
It was under maintenance.

351
00:19:00,222 --> 00:19:04,685
Anyway, I asked the guards
to change all of the locks

352
00:19:04,768 --> 00:19:06,436
here in the mansion.

353
00:19:07,062 --> 00:19:10,899
And, Papa, I just want you
to know that I won't stop

354
00:19:10,983 --> 00:19:13,986
until I find out who did this.

355
00:19:14,069 --> 00:19:15,112
Okay. Okay.

356
00:19:15,195 --> 00:19:16,113
[Emilia] I still can't believe it.

357
00:19:16,196 --> 00:19:18,657
They had some nerve doing this!

358
00:19:18,740 --> 00:19:21,618
They broke into the house
just to place those ants?

359
00:19:21,702 --> 00:19:22,786
[Ivy] Hon?

360
00:19:23,996 --> 00:19:24,997
Hon?

361
00:19:25,372 --> 00:19:26,790
-[Arnaldo] Yes, hon?
-[Ivy] I received your text.

362
00:19:26,874 --> 00:19:27,916
[Ivy] What happened?

363
00:19:28,000 --> 00:19:31,545
-What is she doing here?
-Mom, please. Not now.

364
00:19:31,628 --> 00:19:34,798
Oh, my. Congressman,
could this be an inside job?

365
00:19:34,882 --> 00:19:35,841
[Raul scoffs]

366
00:19:36,383 --> 00:19:37,467
That's possible.

367
00:19:37,551 --> 00:19:39,386
What inside job? That's impossible!

368
00:19:39,469 --> 00:19:42,431
Our employees are loyal to us, Ivy.

369
00:19:42,514 --> 00:19:44,683
Why are you so defensive, Mr. Torillo?

370
00:19:44,766 --> 00:19:45,684
Why are you saying that?

371
00:19:45,767 --> 00:19:47,436
If you have nothing
good to say, just shut up.

372
00:19:47,519 --> 00:19:48,770
[Arnaldo] Enough, Mom.
You have nothing to say--

373
00:19:48,854 --> 00:19:50,439
[Emilia] Why don't you tell her that?

374
00:19:50,522 --> 00:19:51,481
Hon, look.

375
00:19:52,232 --> 00:19:54,776
[Arnaldo] You know, it won't hurt

376
00:19:54,860 --> 00:19:57,654
to run a background check
on our employees.

377
00:19:57,738 --> 00:19:59,406
Better yet, let's replace them all!

378
00:19:59,489 --> 00:20:01,617
And while we're at it,
each and every one of us

379
00:20:01,700 --> 00:20:04,369
should go through a background
check to find out the truth.

380
00:20:04,453 --> 00:20:07,122
But why? We're all family here.

381
00:20:07,623 --> 00:20:10,834
[laughs] No offense, but aside
from the three of us, Mom,

382
00:20:10,918 --> 00:20:13,921
Grandpa, and I, we're
the only true Ardientes.

383
00:20:14,004 --> 00:20:15,172
The rest are excess baggage.

384
00:20:15,255 --> 00:20:16,924
[Raul] You better watch your mouth.

385
00:20:17,007 --> 00:20:17,966
Or else what?

386
00:20:18,050 --> 00:20:18,884
-What?
-[Julio] Stop it!

387
00:20:18,967 --> 00:20:22,429
-Hon.
-[Julio] Shut up, all of you.

388
00:20:22,512 --> 00:20:24,556
Please, please, please!

389
00:20:25,515 --> 00:20:32,147
Raul, just listen to Arnaldo's
suggestion and check it out.

390
00:20:32,231 --> 00:20:34,942
Do whatever needs to be done. Get it done!

391
00:20:35,025 --> 00:20:37,736
Unless you have something to hide.

392
00:20:40,989 --> 00:20:42,115
[chuckles]

393
00:20:44,826 --> 00:20:45,869
[Julio sighs]

394
00:20:51,333 --> 00:20:55,629
[dramatic music playing]

395
00:20:58,131 --> 00:21:00,801
[Marlon] I think that's Miss Camia's car.

396
00:21:01,426 --> 00:21:03,595
[man] It's Miss Camia. Miss Camia!

397
00:21:03,679 --> 00:21:05,472
-[Marlon] She's here.
-[Pandoy] It's Diego.

398
00:21:07,849 --> 00:21:08,892
[Marlon] Ma'am.

399
00:21:09,935 --> 00:21:10,852
Let's go, Diego.

400
00:21:12,271 --> 00:21:13,438
Are you ready?

401
00:21:17,609 --> 00:21:18,652
Uncle, Nanny.

402
00:21:19,027 --> 00:21:21,280
Anyway… Emilia.

403
00:21:22,739 --> 00:21:24,783
Please get my suit ready

404
00:21:24,866 --> 00:21:27,494
because we have to head
to that public appearance.

405
00:21:27,577 --> 00:21:28,662
[Claire scoffs]

406
00:21:28,745 --> 00:21:29,913
No, Papa.

407
00:21:29,997 --> 00:21:32,916
You will just stay home.
It's just one event.

408
00:21:33,000 --> 00:21:35,127
You can attend the others. Just rest.

409
00:21:36,003 --> 00:21:39,172
She's right, Congressman.
It's better for you to rest.

410
00:21:39,256 --> 00:21:41,675
Your condition might worsen
if you insist on going.

411
00:21:41,758 --> 00:21:42,926
[Julio scoffs]

412
00:21:43,010 --> 00:21:45,304
You and your short-sightedness.

413
00:21:46,555 --> 00:21:47,556
You know what?

414
00:21:48,181 --> 00:21:51,977
If I don't attend that event…

415
00:21:52,728 --> 00:21:57,107
our enemies will think that we are weak!

416
00:21:58,191 --> 00:22:03,947
Especially that Diego
and that blasted Jaguar!

417
00:22:04,239 --> 00:22:07,075
They will start feeding on their delusions

418
00:22:07,159 --> 00:22:08,785
and start thinking that,

419
00:22:08,869 --> 00:22:13,332
yes, they have a chance
of beating the Ardientes!

420
00:22:14,750 --> 00:22:19,921
But, anyway, thank you
for your concern, but no thanks.

421
00:22:20,839 --> 00:22:24,426
I am going to that affair.

422
00:22:24,509 --> 00:22:25,969
-Congressman.
-Grandpa!

423
00:22:26,053 --> 00:22:28,055
-I told you, Papa.
-Oh, my!

424
00:22:28,138 --> 00:22:29,306
Just rest.

425
00:22:30,682 --> 00:22:32,809
-What happened?
-So stubborn.

426
00:22:32,893 --> 00:22:34,227
Just rest, Papa. Okay?

427
00:22:34,311 --> 00:22:36,646
-[Claire] Lay down.
-Congressman, please.

428
00:22:37,105 --> 00:22:39,524
I'm asking you. Let us handle it.

429
00:22:39,608 --> 00:22:41,276
Okay? We'll go there on your behalf.

430
00:22:41,359 --> 00:22:43,862
Exactly. We'll make you proud, Papa.

431
00:22:44,988 --> 00:22:49,367
[Julio] Okay, fine. Go. You better.

432
00:22:51,244 --> 00:22:54,039
[pensive music playing]

433
00:22:57,751 --> 00:23:00,921
[Marlon] Everyone, to give
us all a special message,

434
00:23:01,004 --> 00:23:06,009
here's our future governor, Diego Torillo.

435
00:23:06,093 --> 00:23:09,888
[Diego's supporters]
Diego, Diego! Diego, Diego!

436
00:23:09,971 --> 00:23:11,765
Diego, Diego!

437
00:23:11,848 --> 00:23:15,185
Diego, Diego! Diego, Diego!

438
00:23:17,979 --> 00:23:19,272
Friends…

439
00:23:20,941 --> 00:23:23,318
the day we dreamed of has finally arrived.

440
00:23:23,819 --> 00:23:25,904
It's time to file for my candidacy

441
00:23:25,987 --> 00:23:29,783
as the governor of Poblacion Ardiente.

442
00:23:29,866 --> 00:23:33,411
[Diego's supporters]
Diego, Diego! Diego, Diego!

443
00:23:33,495 --> 00:23:35,914
Diego, Diego! Diego…

444
00:23:35,997 --> 00:23:40,418
[Diego] Now's the time
we've all been waiting for!

445
00:23:41,378 --> 00:23:43,839
It's time for us to see the ray of hope

446
00:23:43,922 --> 00:23:44,798
that will put an end

447
00:23:44,881 --> 00:23:48,301
to the dark and corrupt
governance here in Ardiente!

448
00:23:48,385 --> 00:23:49,553
[Arnaldo's supporters] Viva Ardiente!

449
00:23:49,636 --> 00:23:52,556
I will fight for justice!

450
00:23:52,639 --> 00:23:54,724
Viva Ardiente! Viva Ardiente!

451
00:23:54,808 --> 00:23:58,395
-[Marlon] Diego, they're here.
-Diego, Diego! Diego, Diego!

452
00:23:58,478 --> 00:24:01,940
Diego, Diego! Diego, Diego!

453
00:24:02,023 --> 00:24:06,903
Diego, Diego! Diego, Diego! Diego, Diego!

454
00:24:06,987 --> 00:24:11,658
-Viva Ardiente! Viva Ardiente!
-Diego, Diego! Diego, Diego!

455
00:24:11,741 --> 00:24:14,035
-Viva Ardiente!
-Diego, Diego! Diego…

456
00:24:14,119 --> 00:24:16,955
My friends, thank you for coming here

457
00:24:17,038 --> 00:24:18,373
to show your support.

458
00:24:18,456 --> 00:24:22,377
Now, let me hear your loud cheer

459
00:24:22,460 --> 00:24:25,755
for Arnaldo Ardiente-Torillo,

460
00:24:25,839 --> 00:24:28,466
the righteous servant
of Poblacion Ardiente!

461
00:24:28,550 --> 00:24:29,676
Viva Ardiente!

462
00:24:29,759 --> 00:24:36,558
Viva Ardiente! Viva Ardiente!
Viva Ardiente! Viva Ardiente!

463
00:24:36,641 --> 00:24:38,435
I'm Diego Torillo,

464
00:24:38,518 --> 00:24:42,189
your true friend
and ally for a new Ardiente!

465
00:24:42,272 --> 00:24:47,527
Diego, Diego! Diego, Diego! Diego, Diego!

466
00:24:47,611 --> 00:24:49,696
Diego, Diego!

467
00:24:49,779 --> 00:24:54,701
Diego, Diego! Diego, Diego! Diego, Diego!

468
00:24:54,784 --> 00:24:59,664
I'm Arnaldo Ardiente-Torillo,
your righteous servant!

469
00:24:59,748 --> 00:25:01,082
Viva Ardiente!

470
00:25:01,166 --> 00:25:07,255
Viva Ardiente! Viva Ardiente!
Viva Ardiente! Viva Ardiente!

471
00:25:07,339 --> 00:25:12,052
Viva Ardiente!
Viva Ardiente! Viva Ardiente!

472
00:25:12,135 --> 00:25:13,929
The Ardientes?

473
00:25:14,012 --> 00:25:17,098
You're nothing but devious
and greedy criminals!

474
00:25:17,182 --> 00:25:21,895
Let's bring down the Ardientes!
Don't vote for the Ardientes!

475
00:25:21,978 --> 00:25:25,148
-[booing]
-[indistinct chatter]

476
00:25:30,612 --> 00:25:32,530
Camia, Camia, Camia.

477
00:25:32,614 --> 00:25:34,658
Wait, I don't even think I need this.

478
00:25:35,742 --> 00:25:38,745
Did you know that it's not right
to bad-mouth

479
00:25:38,828 --> 00:25:39,913
your political rival?

480
00:25:39,996 --> 00:25:42,415
That's below the belt. Big no-no!

481
00:25:42,499 --> 00:25:45,669
And you even have the guts to lecture me

482
00:25:45,752 --> 00:25:47,254
about attacking below the belt?

483
00:25:47,337 --> 00:25:51,424
Hey, Emilia!
Look at yourself in the mirror.

484
00:25:51,508 --> 00:25:54,094
You are the queen of hired killers

485
00:25:54,177 --> 00:25:56,846
and hired rapists in this place!

486
00:25:57,514 --> 00:26:01,393
Camia, wait. What do you know about me?

487
00:26:01,476 --> 00:26:05,272
Do you have any proof
that I tried to have Ivy Aguas raped?

488
00:26:05,355 --> 00:26:08,191
You know, you don't have common sense.

489
00:26:08,275 --> 00:26:10,402
-Mom, that's enough.
-Wait!

490
00:26:10,485 --> 00:26:13,738
I'm just telling the truth.

491
00:26:13,822 --> 00:26:15,782
This woman doesn't have common sense.

492
00:26:15,865 --> 00:26:19,619
Why would you even think
that Ivy would be supporting us

493
00:26:19,703 --> 00:26:22,372
if she knew that I was the one
who tried to have her raped?

494
00:26:22,455 --> 00:26:25,166
Ivy, come on. Speak up. Why are you here?

495
00:26:26,251 --> 00:26:28,253
[tense music playing]

496
00:26:33,842 --> 00:26:37,846
Of course, I'm only here
to support my Arnaldo.

497
00:26:40,140 --> 00:26:43,810
See? She's a very supportive fiancée.

498
00:26:43,893 --> 00:26:44,769
For all we know,

499
00:26:44,853 --> 00:26:48,732
you might be the ones
who tried to have her raped,

500
00:26:48,815 --> 00:26:51,067
then now, you put the blame on us?

501
00:26:51,151 --> 00:26:52,527
You know, Emilia,

502
00:26:52,610 --> 00:26:55,613
since the start
you've been such a good liar!

503
00:26:56,489 --> 00:26:57,490
[moans]

504
00:26:58,366 --> 00:27:00,285
-Thank you.
-You're welcome!

505
00:27:04,831 --> 00:27:08,543
Do Camia and Diego actually believe…

506
00:27:09,127 --> 00:27:11,296
they can take on the Ardientes?

507
00:27:11,755 --> 00:27:14,007
How ambitious.

508
00:27:14,632 --> 00:27:17,927
And they say there's
no more good TV nowadays.

509
00:27:18,011 --> 00:27:20,096
But this is a really good show.

510
00:27:20,180 --> 00:27:21,264
[chuckles]

511
00:27:21,848 --> 00:27:22,849
Cortez.

512
00:27:24,142 --> 00:27:27,854
Go find Raul.
Tell him I have a job for him.

513
00:27:27,937 --> 00:27:28,938
Yes, Congressman.

514
00:27:30,815 --> 00:27:31,816
[chuckles]

515
00:27:32,776 --> 00:27:33,568
Let's go.

516
00:27:33,651 --> 00:27:36,279
-[man] Viva Ardiente!
-Viva Ardiente! Viva Ardiente!

517
00:27:36,363 --> 00:27:39,282
Viva Ardiente!
Viva Ardiente! Viva Ardiente!

518
00:27:39,366 --> 00:27:41,785
Viva Ardiente! Viva Ardiente!
Viva Ardiente!

519
00:27:41,868 --> 00:27:44,746
-Viva Ardiente!
-Diego, Diego!

520
00:27:44,829 --> 00:27:48,041
-Diego, Diego! Diego, Diego!
-Viva Ardiente! Viva Ardiente!

521
00:27:48,124 --> 00:27:50,752
-Diego, Diego! Diego, Diego!
-Viva Ardiente!

522
00:27:50,835 --> 00:27:53,880
-Viva Ardiente! Viva Ardiente!
-Diego, Diego! Diego, Diego!

523
00:27:53,963 --> 00:27:54,923
[reporter] We're here today

524
00:27:55,006 --> 00:27:56,674
to witness the filing of candidacy

525
00:27:56,758 --> 00:28:00,762
of Arnaldo Ardiente-Torillo
and his half-brother,

526
00:28:00,845 --> 00:28:03,056
Diego Ardiente-Torillo.

527
00:28:05,225 --> 00:28:07,268
[ominous music playing]

528
00:28:11,981 --> 00:28:13,942
[suspenseful music playing]

529
00:28:19,864 --> 00:28:20,865
[Emilia] Hello?

530
00:28:23,743 --> 00:28:25,537
<i>Didn't you tell me…</i>

531
00:28:25,620 --> 00:28:29,165
Diego's party wouldn't make it?

532
00:28:29,249 --> 00:28:30,959
What are they doing here?

533
00:28:31,876 --> 00:28:35,713
Don't worry, Mrs. Emilia.
I'm already working on it.

534
00:28:35,797 --> 00:28:38,049
[sighs] Okay.

535
00:28:48,059 --> 00:28:50,019
[suspenseful music playing]

536
00:29:16,629 --> 00:29:17,672
[dramatic music]

537
00:29:26,890 --> 00:29:27,724
[dramatic music]

538
00:29:47,494 --> 00:29:51,748
-Diego, Diego! Diego, Diego!
-Ardiente!

539
00:29:51,831 --> 00:29:53,666
I had no idea they would
be wearing green today.

540
00:29:53,750 --> 00:29:57,212
And you didn't tell me
our color was maroon. I'm sorry.

541
00:29:57,629 --> 00:29:58,546
It's okay.

542
00:29:58,630 --> 00:30:02,175
Ardiente! Ardiente!
Ardientes are the best!

543
00:30:02,258 --> 00:30:05,804
Ardiente! Ardiente!
Ardientes are the best!

544
00:30:05,887 --> 00:30:09,432
Ardiente! Ardiente!
Ardientes are the best!

545
00:30:09,516 --> 00:30:15,438
Ardiente! Ardiente!
Ardientes are the best!

546
00:30:15,522 --> 00:30:19,025
Ardiente! Ardiente!
Ardientes are the best!

547
00:30:19,108 --> 00:30:22,779
Ardiente! Ardiente!
Ardientes are the best!

548
00:30:24,948 --> 00:30:26,866
[dramatic music playing]

549
00:30:36,876 --> 00:30:37,877
Papa.

550
00:30:38,795 --> 00:30:40,547
Raul, come here. Have a seat.

551
00:30:42,257 --> 00:30:44,175
-[Julio clears throat]
-[Raul exhales]

552
00:30:46,135 --> 00:30:47,011
Yes?

553
00:30:47,637 --> 00:30:51,766
Raul, since all you'll be doing
during the filing

554
00:30:51,850 --> 00:30:55,019
will be putting on a smile
and having your pictures taken,

555
00:30:55,353 --> 00:30:58,523
I realized you're the perfect person

556
00:30:58,606 --> 00:31:02,652
to help me with my little problem.

557
00:31:03,278 --> 00:31:07,240
Thank you for considering me
and calling me here.

558
00:31:07,323 --> 00:31:08,867
[clicks tongue] Of course, of course.

559
00:31:09,576 --> 00:31:11,744
You know, I've come to the conclusion

560
00:31:11,828 --> 00:31:14,163
that there are only
two suspects I can have,

561
00:31:14,247 --> 00:31:17,792
who could possibly be responsible for…

562
00:31:18,376 --> 00:31:19,544
[hisses]

563
00:31:19,627 --> 00:31:22,797
…that fiasco that happened
earlier in my room.

564
00:31:22,881 --> 00:31:23,882
[clears throat]

565
00:31:24,549 --> 00:31:26,759
[Julio] Suspect number one. Diego.

566
00:31:27,343 --> 00:31:29,304
Why? For obvious reasons.

567
00:31:29,387 --> 00:31:32,807
When he was a kid, I let warrior
ants swarm all over him.

568
00:31:32,891 --> 00:31:35,685
Now, he wants revenge.

569
00:31:36,853 --> 00:31:40,315
And a good thing came out of it.
I mean, you've seen it.

570
00:31:40,398 --> 00:31:43,776
If he's the culprit,
that means he grew some balls.

571
00:31:43,860 --> 00:31:46,404
And now he's going against the Ardientes.

572
00:31:47,614 --> 00:31:53,119
But, I don't think he's capable
of doing such…

573
00:31:53,870 --> 00:31:56,873
a dastardly, sneaky act like that.

574
00:31:57,248 --> 00:32:00,168
Which brings me to my second suspect…

575
00:32:00,877 --> 00:32:02,003
Jaguar.

576
00:32:02,086 --> 00:32:03,671
[dramatic music]

577
00:32:03,755 --> 00:32:07,926
I don't know if he's daring
enough to break into my house.

578
00:32:08,009 --> 00:32:14,849
Or if one of our security
personnel is betraying us.

579
00:32:14,933 --> 00:32:17,310
That's why if it's okay with you,

580
00:32:17,769 --> 00:32:20,021
I want you to investigate…

581
00:32:21,105 --> 00:32:22,982
and, if possible,

582
00:32:23,066 --> 00:32:28,863
annihilate this creature
who calls himself "Jaguar".

583
00:32:35,495 --> 00:32:38,498
[tense music playing]

584
00:32:58,059 --> 00:33:01,646
EVEN IF I'M BY THEIR SIDE,
YOU STILL HAVE MY SUPPORT.

585
00:33:10,613 --> 00:33:11,489
[phone dings]

586
00:33:15,535 --> 00:33:17,745
EVEN IF I'M BY THEIR SIDE,
YOU STILL HAVE MY SUPPORT.

587
00:33:26,838 --> 00:33:30,299
-I'm sorry I'm late, Diego.
-Nimfa, what took you so long?

588
00:33:31,884 --> 00:33:34,721
I was embarrassed
to show myself to Aunt Camia.

589
00:33:34,804 --> 00:33:36,305
I thought she was still mad at me.

590
00:33:37,640 --> 00:33:40,351
What? Why? What happened?

591
00:33:40,852 --> 00:33:43,271
Diego, let's talk about it later.

592
00:33:46,232 --> 00:33:48,234
[suspenseful music plays]

593
00:33:49,235 --> 00:33:50,403
[line ringing]

594
00:33:51,070 --> 00:33:51,904
Hello.

595
00:33:52,488 --> 00:33:53,489
<i>Rufo.</i>

596
00:33:55,116 --> 00:33:56,868
<i>I'm going to your hideout.</i>

597
00:33:56,951 --> 00:34:00,872
Before I get there, you need to be gone.

598
00:34:01,247 --> 00:34:03,041
<i>Because Julio gave me an order.</i>

599
00:34:03,124 --> 00:34:06,169
He ordered me to annihilate
every one of you.

600
00:34:06,252 --> 00:34:08,880
Jaguar… Relax.

601
00:34:09,505 --> 00:34:11,132
<i>We don't need to leave.</i>

602
00:34:11,632 --> 00:34:15,386
All we need to do
is prepare for their arrival.

603
00:34:22,393 --> 00:34:25,646
-[clapping]
-[camera clicks]

604
00:34:27,857 --> 00:34:29,859
[ominous music playing]

605
00:34:34,739 --> 00:34:35,615
[camera clicks]

606
00:34:35,698 --> 00:34:38,534
-I think it's our turn.
-Let's go, Diego. This is it.

607
00:34:38,618 --> 00:34:41,204
It's official.
Your dream's about to come true.

608
00:34:41,871 --> 00:34:43,039
Thank you, Uncle.

609
00:34:45,875 --> 00:34:48,086
-Congratulations.
-Thank you very much.

610
00:34:49,253 --> 00:34:51,172
-[Arnaldo] Let's go.
-[Loring] This is it.

611
00:34:59,263 --> 00:35:02,225
[suspenseful music playing]

612
00:35:45,393 --> 00:35:48,146
-[Pandoy and Loring laugh]
-Thank you. Thank you.

613
00:35:48,229 --> 00:35:49,272
-[man] Mrs. Loring.
-What?

614
00:35:49,355 --> 00:35:51,232
-I need to tell you something.
-What?

615
00:35:51,858 --> 00:35:53,651
[man] Your house is burning.

616
00:35:53,734 --> 00:35:54,902
-[Pandoy] What?
-[man] It's burning.

617
00:35:54,986 --> 00:35:55,736
[man] Come on!

618
00:35:55,820 --> 00:35:59,407
Diego, our house is burning down.

619
00:35:59,490 --> 00:36:02,660
What? Marlon, you stay here.

620
00:36:02,743 --> 00:36:04,787
I need to make sure nobody got hurt.

621
00:36:04,871 --> 00:36:06,038
-[Marlon] Yes.
-Aunt Camia.

622
00:36:06,789 --> 00:36:09,542
[Marlon] I'm sorry, but we have
to leave. Thanks again.

623
00:36:12,837 --> 00:36:14,839
[tense music playing]

624
00:36:23,139 --> 00:36:25,308
[Loring sobbing]

625
00:36:25,391 --> 00:36:28,144
-Wait. [screams]
-Loring… What?

626
00:36:30,479 --> 00:36:31,981
[Loring wailing]

627
00:36:32,857 --> 00:36:34,400
[Pandoy] Loring…

628
00:36:36,569 --> 00:36:40,198
[Pandoy] Loring, what about the funds?

629
00:36:41,574 --> 00:36:44,076
-[Pandoy stammering]
-[Loring wailing]

630
00:36:44,744 --> 00:36:48,748
-[Pandoy] Where'd you keep the--
-Pandoy… Pandoy.

631
00:36:48,831 --> 00:36:52,710
[Loring] We lost all our money!

632
00:36:52,793 --> 00:36:54,670
[Loring sobbing]

633
00:36:55,421 --> 00:36:56,589
Diego…

634
00:36:56,672 --> 00:36:58,549
Pandoy, this wasn't an accident.

635
00:36:59,175 --> 00:37:02,053
They made it look like
the house caught fire,

636
00:37:02,136 --> 00:37:03,888
but they took our money!

637
00:37:03,971 --> 00:37:06,224
They took everything!

638
00:37:07,266 --> 00:37:08,893
[wailing]

639
00:37:09,852 --> 00:37:10,853
[Marlon] Diego…

640
00:37:11,354 --> 00:37:14,732
All our campaign materials caught on fire.

641
00:37:18,903 --> 00:37:21,864
They burned it all.

642
00:37:22,615 --> 00:37:26,786
I know you're all devastated.
I'm devastated too.

643
00:37:26,869 --> 00:37:29,622
It's hard to see
all our hard work turn to ash.

644
00:37:30,748 --> 00:37:34,877
Marlon, schedule our meeting
with Senator Magno.

645
00:37:34,961 --> 00:37:36,545
Okay, Diego. I'll take care of it.

646
00:37:37,255 --> 00:37:38,798
[Loring sobbing]

647
00:37:38,881 --> 00:37:40,299
Those bastards!

648
00:37:43,886 --> 00:37:48,057
[Loring sobbing]

649
00:37:48,349 --> 00:37:50,393
[dramatic music playing]

650
00:37:50,977 --> 00:37:52,395
We'll get back at them. They'll pay.

651
00:37:57,233 --> 00:37:59,026
[man] Boss, we're all set.

652
00:38:00,736 --> 00:38:02,697
[suspenseful music playing]

653
00:38:15,376 --> 00:38:16,460
[phone ringing]

654
00:38:18,879 --> 00:38:19,880
Do it now.

655
00:38:20,256 --> 00:38:21,257
All right.

656
00:38:33,477 --> 00:38:34,854
[dramatic music]

657
00:38:39,900 --> 00:38:41,861
[gunfire]

658
00:38:57,293 --> 00:38:59,045
[loud explosion]

659
00:38:59,879 --> 00:39:01,464
[tense music playing]

660
00:39:22,735 --> 00:39:25,321
[dramatic music]

661
00:39:28,657 --> 00:39:29,742
They planned it.

662
00:39:30,451 --> 00:39:32,661
They knew we were busy
with the filing and rally,

663
00:39:32,745 --> 00:39:34,205
so that's when they attacked our place.

664
00:39:34,830 --> 00:39:38,125
They've always played dirty!

665
00:39:39,210 --> 00:39:42,630
But, how did they know
where we hid our funds?

666
00:39:43,839 --> 00:39:45,966
Don't you think they have a spy here?

667
00:39:47,593 --> 00:39:49,345
[ominous music playing]

668
00:39:49,678 --> 00:39:53,432
An ally of the Ardientes
who watches our every move.

669
00:39:55,267 --> 00:39:56,227
[sighs]

670
00:40:00,356 --> 00:40:02,858
Diego, I'm sorry.

671
00:40:03,859 --> 00:40:05,736
I know she's your friend…

672
00:40:05,820 --> 00:40:08,823
but I can't help
but be suspicious of Nimfa.

673
00:40:08,906 --> 00:40:11,617
I caught her going through my things.

674
00:40:11,700 --> 00:40:15,287
She said her father was sick,
and she badly needed money.

675
00:40:16,372 --> 00:40:18,791
Are you saying Nimfa stole our funds?

676
00:40:19,375 --> 00:40:20,376
[sighs]

677
00:40:20,835 --> 00:40:22,169
I'm not sure, Diego.

678
00:40:22,253 --> 00:40:24,380
It's just that with the turn of events,

679
00:40:24,463 --> 00:40:26,424
I feel like something's off about her.

680
00:40:26,507 --> 00:40:29,802
[suspenseful music playing]

681
00:40:33,848 --> 00:40:37,810
Miss Camia. Are you suggesting I did this?

682
00:40:38,394 --> 00:40:39,437
Nimfa.

683
00:40:40,062 --> 00:40:42,148
You already gave me another chance,

684
00:40:42,231 --> 00:40:43,858
and I won't throw it away.

685
00:40:45,484 --> 00:40:50,948
I just did that because I was
really desperate then.

686
00:40:51,031 --> 00:40:53,117
[crying]

687
00:40:53,200 --> 00:40:54,243
[Diego] Nimfa…

688
00:40:55,703 --> 00:40:57,830
You're my friend so I trust you.

689
00:40:58,122 --> 00:41:00,040
But we can't trust the Ardientes.

690
00:41:00,749 --> 00:41:02,877
We're just worried about you.

691
00:41:03,502 --> 00:41:04,503
What if…

692
00:41:06,630 --> 00:41:09,175
What if the Ardientes
really are using you?

693
00:41:09,842 --> 00:41:11,844
I'm not their lapdog!

694
00:41:11,927 --> 00:41:15,806
[scoffs] How could you
even think of that, Diego?

695
00:41:15,890 --> 00:41:18,100
We've been friends for so long.

696
00:41:19,351 --> 00:41:21,770
But it's fine if that's
what you think of me,

697
00:41:21,854 --> 00:41:23,606
I'll just leave Miss Camia's place.

698
00:41:24,231 --> 00:41:26,859
I don't want to lose your trust.

699
00:41:26,942 --> 00:41:32,072
Nimfa… Don't say that.
I can't let you lose your job.

700
00:41:32,615 --> 00:41:34,909
Because you have to help your father.

701
00:41:35,743 --> 00:41:37,661
So, you don't have to quit.

702
00:41:37,745 --> 00:41:40,539
[suspenseful music playing]

703
00:41:42,833 --> 00:41:47,421
Thank you, Miss Camia.
I won't ever do that again.

704
00:41:48,214 --> 00:41:51,467
I'll cut my hands myself
if I ever do it again.

705
00:41:52,801 --> 00:41:55,179
I promise I will never break your trust.

706
00:41:55,971 --> 00:41:57,014
Thank you.

707
00:42:10,402 --> 00:42:13,030
[Emilia] Come, Aunt Claire.
You have to see this.

708
00:42:13,614 --> 00:42:16,784
-[Claire] What is it?
-We have to check it out.

709
00:42:17,284 --> 00:42:18,285
Okay.

710
00:42:20,871 --> 00:42:21,914
Money.

711
00:42:25,000 --> 00:42:26,961
Money again. Boring.

712
00:42:28,504 --> 00:42:30,422
This, Aunt Claire…

713
00:42:32,716 --> 00:42:34,593
Hmm… Check.

714
00:42:35,427 --> 00:42:41,267
Through this, we will prove
if Ivy Aguas is Camia's backer.

715
00:42:41,350 --> 00:42:42,101
[chuckles]

716
00:42:42,184 --> 00:42:47,398
We can finally put an end
to Ivy Aguas' betrayal.

717
00:42:48,357 --> 00:42:49,900
What can I say?

718
00:42:50,859 --> 00:42:52,152
Good job, Emilia.

719
00:42:52,736 --> 00:42:55,030
-Well thank you, Aunt Claire.
-[Claire chuckles]

720
00:42:55,990 --> 00:42:58,367
-[Claire] Well done.
-So, what are we celebrating?

721
00:42:58,826 --> 00:43:02,746
Well, aside from that thing with Diego,

722
00:43:02,830 --> 00:43:04,665
I just got some information

723
00:43:04,748 --> 00:43:07,293
that they're headed to Senator Magno,

724
00:43:07,376 --> 00:43:10,629
so you have to set up an
appointment and beat them to it.

725
00:43:11,297 --> 00:43:12,298
Okay, sure.

726
00:43:12,381 --> 00:43:13,716
-[Ivy] Hon?
-Hon?

727
00:43:13,799 --> 00:43:18,762
[Ivy] Oh, were you guys talking?
What was it about?

728
00:43:18,846 --> 00:43:20,431
Oh. Sorry, Ivy.

729
00:43:20,514 --> 00:43:23,350
It's strictly for family members
only, so we can't tell you.

730
00:43:24,226 --> 00:43:28,731
Mom, Ivy's practically part
of the family already.

731
00:43:29,189 --> 00:43:30,816
Part of the family?

732
00:43:31,358 --> 00:43:34,528
Wow, how can that be
when she's accusing me

733
00:43:34,612 --> 00:43:36,322
of being the mastermind of her rape?

734
00:43:37,698 --> 00:43:38,949
Hon, let me.

735
00:43:39,617 --> 00:43:43,829
Oh, Emilia, did you already
forget what I did earlier?

736
00:43:43,912 --> 00:43:47,583
Didn't I put on an act with you
in front of a lot of people

737
00:43:47,666 --> 00:43:49,918
even though you're blaming the other party

738
00:43:50,002 --> 00:43:53,881
for something you yourself planned?

739
00:43:56,634 --> 00:43:57,635
[exhales]

740
00:43:58,469 --> 00:44:01,930
Okay, you know what? Let's stop this.

741
00:44:02,431 --> 00:44:04,725
I'm doing this for Arnaldo, and…

742
00:44:05,392 --> 00:44:08,187
besides, you're going to be
my mother-in-law.

743
00:44:08,270 --> 00:44:13,150
I know we had some conflicts
these past few days, but…

744
00:44:14,485 --> 00:44:17,279
I've had enough of this,
my future mother-in-law.

745
00:44:17,363 --> 00:44:19,615
So, I was hoping
we could go back to being okay.

746
00:44:20,491 --> 00:44:21,492
[sighs]

747
00:44:28,749 --> 00:44:30,125
Thank you, mother-in-law.

748
00:44:32,252 --> 00:44:33,796
Okay, we're good.

749
00:44:43,013 --> 00:44:46,850
-Mamita.
-So, who apologized first?

750
00:44:47,685 --> 00:44:48,894
Oh.

751
00:44:48,977 --> 00:44:51,397
Future mother-in-law,
that's not important.

752
00:44:51,480 --> 00:44:53,899
-Congressman.
-[Julio] Look at that.

753
00:44:54,858 --> 00:44:59,405
Such a beautiful portrait.
Future mother-in-law

754
00:44:59,488 --> 00:45:03,575
and daughter-in-law in each other's arms.

755
00:45:03,659 --> 00:45:04,701
[Emilia and Ivy chuckling]

756
00:45:05,285 --> 00:45:07,788
A while ago, they were
at each other's throats.

757
00:45:07,871 --> 00:45:09,540
[Emilia] I know.

758
00:45:09,623 --> 00:45:13,252
[Julio] Women are the hardest
creatures to understand.

759
00:45:13,335 --> 00:45:16,588
Well, Papa, did you see
what happened to Diego today?

760
00:45:16,672 --> 00:45:21,510
Oh, yes. And I'm so proud of all of you.

761
00:45:22,970 --> 00:45:25,180
Seems like everybody's
in each other's arms

762
00:45:25,264 --> 00:45:28,392
and waving peace signs at each other.

763
00:45:28,475 --> 00:45:32,020
Maybe we can celebrate
as one family again?

764
00:45:32,104 --> 00:45:33,147
That would be great, Papa.

765
00:45:33,230 --> 00:45:36,567
Perfect timing
because I had dinner prepared.

766
00:45:36,650 --> 00:45:39,987
Oh, good. I'm famished. Let's go?

767
00:45:40,070 --> 00:45:42,489
[Emilia] Let's go.
Let's all have dinner together.

768
00:45:42,573 --> 00:45:44,908
[phone rings]

769
00:45:44,992 --> 00:45:46,493
[Emilia] What's for dinner?

770
00:45:47,786 --> 00:45:48,745
Hello?

771
00:45:48,829 --> 00:45:52,416
[Raul] <i>Papa. Looks like Jaguar</i>
<i>got ahead of us.</i>

772
00:45:52,499 --> 00:45:54,877
<i>Most of our men were killed.</i>

773
00:45:55,461 --> 00:45:57,838
-What?!
-Papa?

774
00:45:58,839 --> 00:46:00,507
-Yes…
-[Emilia] What's going on?

775
00:46:00,591 --> 00:46:03,552
I'll call you later. Nothing. [chuckles]

776
00:46:03,635 --> 00:46:07,556
Just some shocking news I heard.
Everything's fine.

777
00:46:07,639 --> 00:46:11,018
It's just that I left something
in the office.

778
00:46:11,101 --> 00:46:13,312
I'll just go and get it. I'll be back.

779
00:46:13,395 --> 00:46:15,189
Make sure you join us for dinner, Papa.

780
00:46:15,272 --> 00:46:17,483
-Yeah, for sure.
-[Emilia] All right.

781
00:46:19,151 --> 00:46:22,404
[Emilia] Help yourselves. Come
on. Sit down. Let's have dinner.

782
00:46:22,488 --> 00:46:23,530
[Julio screams]

783
00:46:25,908 --> 00:46:26,950
[screams]

784
00:46:30,746 --> 00:46:34,208
You bastard! Jaguar, you bastard!

785
00:46:34,791 --> 00:46:37,503
-Domingo! Get in here!
-[Domingo] Congressman.

786
00:46:39,046 --> 00:46:42,049
I held back for far too long

787
00:46:42,841 --> 00:46:44,593
from those bastards.

788
00:46:44,676 --> 00:46:48,430
Find the families of all our former men

789
00:46:48,514 --> 00:46:51,099
who betrayed us and sided with Jaguar.

790
00:46:51,183 --> 00:46:51,975
Yes, Congressman.

791
00:46:52,059 --> 00:46:56,146
It's time for me to teach them a lesson,

792
00:46:56,230 --> 00:47:00,817
so they will know
the wrath of Julio Ardiente!

793
00:47:01,735 --> 00:47:02,736
Go!

794
00:47:04,988 --> 00:47:05,989
[groans]

795
00:47:08,492 --> 00:47:10,619
[dramatic music playing]

796
00:47:13,956 --> 00:47:16,542
[Ivy] <i>There's a spy in Diego's camp?</i>

797
00:47:16,625 --> 00:47:17,793
<i>We're a political family,</i>

798
00:47:17,876 --> 00:47:20,921
<i>and we have been doing this</i>
<i>for many, many years.</i>

799
00:47:21,004 --> 00:47:22,965
[Emilia] <i>I'm giving you until tonight</i>

800
00:47:23,048 --> 00:47:25,551
<i>to finish your job.</i>

801
00:47:25,634 --> 00:47:27,928
<i>Or else… Do you see that toilet?</i>

802
00:47:28,011 --> 00:47:29,805
<i>That's the last thing</i>

803
00:47:29,888 --> 00:47:32,891
<i>you'll see before you die,</i>
<i>you piece of shit!</i>

804
00:47:32,975 --> 00:47:37,646
[Camia] <i>Lily, thanks for helping</i>
<i>out with Diego's campaign.</i>

805
00:47:37,729 --> 00:47:39,064
[Emilia] <i>Do you have an update on Camia?</i>

806
00:47:39,147 --> 00:47:40,857
<i>Lily Cruz is alive.</i>

807
00:47:46,947 --> 00:47:49,908
[theme music playing]
